{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015620-who-are-the-deep-lords-of-misrule","id":1015620,"title":"who are the deep lords of misrule?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-11T02:46:57-08:00","id":1015620,"title":"who are the deep lords of misrule?","content":"if im not mistaken this term appears in the path of screams infernalism.<br /> <br /> its in a chart showing the infernalist heirarchy of &quot;gods&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T04:09:34-08:00","id":1015637,"title":"","content":"That book is also the only time they are mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T11:53:51-08:00","id":1016181,"title":"","content":"I recall taking the term as synonymous with demon lords, Maeljin incarnae, and major Outsider presences, i.e. the assorted big patrons of the Nephandi rather than their subordinates and canon fodder. But I don't know if I just based that on an impression or if it was from specific bit of text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T12:28:42-08:00","id":1016196,"title":"","content":"The glossary in the book says this:<br /> <br /> <b>Deep Lords of Misrule:</b> Legendary \u201cghost-oracles\u201d of darkness and chaos. Sentient fragments of the Primal Void, said to occupy a null-space beyond the heavens and the gods. Sometimes regarded as the breaths of the Absolute, its attendants, or both.<br /> <br /> Page 46 calls them &quot;the fabled Ghost-Oracles of metaphysical Oblivion&quot; and links them to possible Descension.<br /> <br /> \u200bPage 81 says that they are &quot;entities who glide in perfect orbit around the Absolute until all Creation returns to primordial Darkness and the Absolute is sated at last.&quot; This is in connection to the Absolute being the Tenth Sphere.<br /> <br /> \u200bPage 104 has the little chart you're referring to - it ranks them directly below the Absolute and the Triat.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's a lot you can do with this. I'll be honest, the first things they make me think of are the Neverborn.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T23:36:32-08:00","id":1016427,"title":"","content":"They could be rulers/owners/chief inhabitants of the Qlippoths (assuming that Qlippoths are some other worlds). One for each of the Spheres..though the deeper truth is perhaps that they are more of them. Wikipedia lists <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qliphoth\" target=\"_blank\">ten</a> Qlipphoths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 03-12-2018, 06:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T06:40:53-08:00","id":1016520,"title":"","content":"For which game line are you trying to answer the question?<br /> <br /> If Werewolf - it needs to be part of the Wyrm, since the Wyrm is the source of all corruption and destruction in the universe. Even if these Deep Lords of Misrule weren't created by the Wyrm, by their actions they serve it and so they are part and parcel with it. Look at the Talons of the Wyrm, Maeljin, etc.<br /> <br /> If Wraith - you sort of need to do the Neverborn here.<br /> <br /> If Vampire - uhh, whatever it is the Baali serve? <br /> <br /> If Demon - pick a few Earthbound.<br /> <br /> Mage of course can play well with any of these, and can add some more. Your problem is that various cWoD gamelines all created their own Cthulhu-esque monsters, and Mage can accommodate any of them - so Mage ends up with like eight options for Cthulhu. It's not really a question of what specifically the book is referring to, so much as what you are going to interpret them as referring to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T09:06:25-08:00","id":1016583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015620-who-are-the-deep-lords-of-misrule?p=1016196#post1016196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The glossary in the book says this:<br /> <br /> <b>Deep Lords of Misrule:</b> Legendary \u201cghost-oracles\u201d of darkness and chaos. Sentient fragments of the Primal Void, said to occupy a null-space beyond the heavens and the gods. Sometimes regarded as the breaths of the Absolute, its attendants, or both.<br /> <br /> Page 46 calls them &quot;the fabled Ghost-Oracles of metaphysical Oblivion&quot; and links them to possible Descension.<br /> <br /> \u200bPage 81 says that they are &quot;entities who glide in perfect orbit around the Absolute until all Creation returns to primordial Darkness and the Absolute is sated at last.&quot; This is in connection to the Absolute being the Tenth Sphere.<br /> <br /> \u200bPage 104 has the little chart you're referring to - it ranks them directly below the Absolute and the Triat.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's a lot you can do with this. I'll be honest, the first things they make me think of are the Neverborn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> it also lists urge wyrms below them though. that's a bit problematic for me because i see the urge wyrms and the neverborn as the same beings.<br /> <br /> at any rate the urge wyrms are celestines(in power if nothing else)<br /> the neverborn(even if we see them as different beings) are strong...but not stronger than lucifer or fucking YHWH also known as &quot; first and mightiest child of the One&quot;<br /> <br /> thus based on that description i'dsay they represent the triatic &quot;wyrm&quot; for instance grandmother(or eater of souls given that they seem identical)<br /> <br /> edit:<br /> alternatively(as i read these pages) it's possible the deep lords of misrule have several tiers of strength?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 12-13-2016, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T09:24:55-08:00","id":1016595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015620-who-are-the-deep-lords-of-misrule?p=1016520#post1016520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Demon - pick a few Earthbound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than Earthbound demons I'd go for the really major ones still trapped in the Abyss, as there seems to be an otherdimensional aspect implied.<br /> <br /> I thought urge wyrms were also incarnae, just more diffuse and conceptual than the Maeljin Incarnae that personify them? My (admittedly out of date) read was that only Beast-of-War, Eater-of-Souls, and the Defiler Wyrm were celestines.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:01:22-08:00","id":1016667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015620-who-are-the-deep-lords-of-misrule?p=1016583#post1016583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> it also lists urge wyrms below them though. that's a bit problematic for me because i see the urge wyrms and the neverborn as the same beings.<br /> <br /> at any rate the urge wyrms are celestines(in power if nothing else)<br /> the neverborn(even if we see them as different beings) are strong...but not stronger than lucifer or fucking YHWH also known as &quot; first and mightiest child of the One&quot;<br /> <br /> thus based on that description i'dsay they represent the triatic &quot;wyrm&quot; for instance grandmother(or eater of souls given that they seem identical)<br /> <br /> edit:<br /> alternatively(as i read these pages) it's possible the deep lords of misrule have several tiers of strength?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe descriptions of the Absolute made me think of Grandmother, actually, which is one of the reasons I thought of the Neverborn. If you go with the idea of Grandmother (or the Absolute) being some sort of anti-God, then they're as powerful as you want them to be. Lucifer might not even exist in your WoD, so it's totally your call. And if you're riffing on the idea that the Malfeans of the middle Umbra are the dreams of the underworld Malfeans, then they can totally have several tiers of strength, one of which might indeed be the Triat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T06:09:21-08:00","id":1017613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015620-who-are-the-deep-lords-of-misrule?p=1016667#post1016667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThe descriptions of the Absolute made me think of Grandmother, actually, which is one of the reasons I thought of the Neverborn. If you go with the idea of Grandmother (or the Absolute) being some sort of anti-God, then they're as powerful as you want them to be. Lucifer might not even exist in your WoD, so it's totally your call. And if you're riffing on the idea that the Malfeans of the middle Umbra are the dreams of the underworld Malfeans, then they can totally have several tiers of strength, one of which might indeed be the Triat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> personally i see the maejin incarna as either a special class of onceborn(the maejin are former humans afterall) or something like that. not dreams of the neverborn.<br /> after all the book of madness says that after some neverborn awakened the malfean nephandi were the ones who suffered the least.<br /> <br /> the problem with grandmother being the absolute is (in my view) her relative weakness . sure she can destroy earth but at that power scale this may not mean much. plus the strongest neverborn is almost as strong as she is.<br /> <br /> thus i view her as eater of souls her desires are similar to those of the absolute though not identical i think","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}